messages:
tasha: OrchidHealth asked for a one-page presales runbook: ephemeral handshake for hosted, recommended streaming knobs to avoid client/backpressure issues, how tool/function calls appear and how to reply, plus a copy-paste curl + tiny node snippet. Also a conservative cost hint for ~40 rps @ ~1k tokens avg. Can we assemble? :wave:
devon: Hosted POC initially. Short checklist: 1) POST to presales ephemeral endpoint to mint short-lived token; 2) use SDK credentialProvider to refresh tokens; 3) open WS with subprotocol `rwd-stream-v1`; 4) send initial `meta` frame with `schema_id`; 5) listen for `toolcall` events and reply with `tool_response` frames; 6) if you see sustained high concurrency switch to batch REST.
sri: Streaming knobs I usually give: max_inflight=6, heartbeat=20s, client-side inflight queue, exponential backoff with jitter on 429s (base 150ms). For multiplexed clients set multiplex=true and limit concurrent streams per connection. Add server-side prefix caching for repeated prompts to cut token spend.
devon: Minimal handshake curl (presales dev):
```bash
curl -sS -X POST https://presales.redwood.ai/v1/ephemeral \ 
  -H "Authorization: Bearer PRESALES_KEY" \ 
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \ 
  -d '{"account":"orchidhealth","purpose":"poc"}'
# -> {"token":"ey...","expires_in":900}
```
sri: Tiny Node snippet to paste into their repo:
```js
const client = new RedwoodClient({ credentialProvider: async () => ({ token: await fetchEphemeral() }), streaming: true });
const stream = await client.stream({ model: 'rwd-4-small', multiplex: true });
stream.send({ type: 'meta', schema_id: 'orchid-v1', strict: true });
stream.on('message', async (msg) => {
  if (msg.type === 'toolcall') {
    const out = await callBookingService(msg.args);
    stream.send({ type: 'tool_response', id: msg.id, result: out });
  }
  if (msg.type === 'chunk') { /* append tokens to buffer */ }
});
```
tasha: Nice. Can we include a one-line note about structured output validation?
devon: Add: "Include a JSON Schema in the meta frame or request body; set `strict:true` to enable server-side validation. SDK emits `schema_violation` events for regressions and `schema_valid` events when outputs match"
finance: Cost hint: 40 rps * ~1k tokens ≈ 3.5B tokens/day if run 24/7. For a business-hours POC (8h/day) ~1.2B tokens. Hosted POC costs vary by model and caching; recommend a 1-hour representative run to measure real tokenization. Conservative ballpark for a short POC: low thousands USD, but DM me for a model-specific quote.
ops-bot: presales/runbooks updated: orchidhealth-poc.md (uploaded) :white_check_mark:
tasha: Perfect 139 I'll paste this into the customer onboarding doc and book a 30m demo. If they ask about SOC2/KMS we'll loop security. Thanks team! :thumbsup:
